From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:35:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] librustutils: system_properties and users under
 atl_android_userspace

ATL builds device Rust for the host triple (target_os = linux) and
provides bionic system properties in its C library, so the modules the
ATL Android-userspace build needs are enabled by its --cfg. users is
enabled too because keystore2 derives user and app ids from uids with
it, and its body is only arithmetic over libcutils AID constants.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ATL-specific cfg]
Patch-Reason: target_os is the host OS on ATL; only the source gate can tell this build apart, the converter passes the cfg
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 lib.rs | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib.rs b/lib.rs
index a1beab553174229f073edc243178826f35fb1af2..7658dd8a12f435e1406bb61074380aa0010965c3 100644
--- a/lib.rs
+++ b/lib.rs
@@ -17,10 +17,10 @@
 #[cfg(target_os = "android")]
 pub mod sockets;
 
-#[cfg(target_os = "android")]
+#[cfg(any(target_os = "android", atl_android_userspace))]
 pub mod system_properties;
 
-#[cfg(target_os = "android")]
+#[cfg(any(target_os = "android", atl_android_userspace))]
 pub mod users;
 
 pub mod inherited_fd;
